{
  "info": {
    "name": "FAFCare API (fixed - real MFA login flow)",
    "_postman_id": "fafcare-api-collection-fixed",
    "description": "Rebuilt from the actual backend source (authController.js, server.js, validation.js, seed.js). The original collection assumed a single-step /api/auth/login that returns a token directly and used hand-typed JWTs with fake signatures - both are why every request 401'd. This version logs in for real (login -> MFA -> token) and pulls real seeded IDs from the public catalog endpoints instead of guessing UUIDs. Run folder 0 first.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Setup - Login & Get Real Tokens (run this folder first, top to bottom)",
      "description": "This API does NOT issue a token from a single /api/auth/login call. Login is two steps: (1) POST /api/auth/login checks the password and returns an mfaToken, (2) POST /api/auth/verify-mfa checks a 6-digit OTP and returns the real JWT. The OTP is only present in step 1's response if the backend has MFA_RETURN_OTP=true in its .env; otherwise it is printed to the backend's console log (or emailed if SMTP is configured) and you must paste it into the *_otp variable by hand. NOTE: /api/auth/* is rate-limited to 5 requests per 15 minutes PER IP, shared across login/verify-mfa/register/resend-mfa. Running this whole folder repeatedly will get you 429s until the window resets or the backend restarts - see the chat answer for how to raise this for local testing.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login Step 1 - Patient",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{patient_email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{patient_password}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.environment.set('patient_password', (pm.environment.get('seed_password') || 'Password123!') + '-Patient-' + pm.environment.get('patient_csv_id') + '!');"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Login step 1 returns 200 (credentials accepted)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.environment.set('patient_mfa_token', json.mfaToken);",
                  "    if (json.otpCode) {",
                  "        pm.environment.set('patient_otp', json.otpCode);",
                  "    } else {",
                  "        console.warn('Patient: no otpCode in response. Set MFA_RETURN_OTP=true in the backend .env for automated Postman testing, or copy the 6-digit code the backend logs to its console and paste it into the patient_otp environment variable by hand, then re-run the Verify MFA request.');",
                  "    }",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.error('Patient login step 1 failed:', pm.response.text());",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify MFA - Patient",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/verify-mfa",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "verify-mfa"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"mfaToken\": \"{{patient_mfa_token}}\",\n  \"otpCode\": \"{{patient_otp}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('MFA verification returns 200 (token issued)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.environment.set('patient_jwt', json.token);",
                  "    pm.environment.set('jwt_token', json.token); // primary/default token used by generic requests",
                  "    if (json.user.patient_id) pm.environment.set('patient_id', json.user.patient_id);",
                  "    if (json.user.doctor_id) pm.environment.set('patient_id', json.user.doctor_id);",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.error('Patient MFA verification failed:', pm.response.text());",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
